==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|outside|er}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌaʊtˈsaɪdəɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outsider.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is not part of a [[community]] or [[organization]].
#: {{ux|en|While the initiated easily understand the symbols, they are wholly inaccessible to '''outsiders'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2004
|last=Carlin
|first=George
|authorlink=George Carlin
|chapter=Preface
|title={{w|When Will Jesus Bring the Pork Chops?}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/sacredmountainof0000john/
|location=[[New York]]
|publisher={{w|Hyperion Books}}
|ISBN=1-4013-0821-X
|OCLC=757869006
|OL=24604921M
|page=[https://archive.org/details/whenwilljesusbri00hype/page/n14/]
|text=I'm an '''outsider''' by choice, but not truly. It's the unpleasantness of the system that keeps me out. I'd rather be in, in a good system. That's where my discontent comes from: being forced to choose to stay outside.}}
# A [[newcomer]] with little or no experience in an organization or community.
#: {{ux|en|Seeing the mess professional politicians have made of things is it any wonder the electorate is beginning to prefer '''outsiders'''?}}
#*{{quote-video game|en||developer={{w|BioWare}}|title={{w|Mass Effect: Andromeda}}|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2017|platform=PC|scene=Legacy|oclc=1261299044|text=These worlds have always belonged to us, from the moment our ancestors saw them through ancient telescopes. We claimed them when our first explorers reached the stars, and they remained our worlds even after the Scourge divided us in darkness. '''Outsiders''' have no right to these treasures, and true angara must stand ready to defend our birthright.}}
# A [[competitor]] or [[contestant]] who has little [[chance]] of [[winning]]; a [[long shot]].
#: {{ux|en|Johnny was an '''outsider''' at this year's karate tournament, but he still managed to win second place out of sheer determination.}}

